id: pm-iceees
title: Retain tested optional-peer closures in the published runtime bundle
description: PR1495 installed Node22/24 consumers on Linux/macOS/Windows and the npm smoke all refuse the packed Sentry10.76.2 closure because has-flag is absent. pnpm11.28.5 records supports-color as an optional peer of debug; the producer stages every locked package but npm packlist intentionally skips peer edges and omits that peer subtree. Qualify and publish the complete tested closure with source manifests preserved. This is a newly exposed packaging boundary and not a claim of historical user-facing loss.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:32:31.483Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T04:35:31.400Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T04:35:30.617Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T04:35:30.617Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: A real npm archive fixture reproduces the missing optional-peer subtree before the fix; publication projects exact tested peer bindings without source mutation; installed runtime and Node/Bun/npx/bunx smokes and unchanged artifact/security/coverage gates pass.
parent: pm-998juj
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Project missing tested peer bindings into staged runtime manifests and write each changed manifest once; preserve installed/source bytes and strict closure verification.
expected_result: Every package selected by the tested runtime ledger survives the real npm archive and installed Node/Bun consumers; missing peer leaves fail closed.
actual_result: "Real tarball fixtures reproduce the original omission and now resolve peer/leaf chains with source manifests preserved; deliberate leaf removal refuses. Linked archive/runtime-lock checks pass after review refactor. Six hosted Node22.18/24 Linux/macOS/Windows first-run jobs, npm/npx/Bun/bunx smokes and exact100/100/100/100 coverage passed in CI39096420681; final review/closure commit remains subject to unchanged required checks."
